## 5. Investigate the extended mind

Examine how the public work relates AI collaboration to earlier forms of
externalized human thought, such as:

- notebooks
- maps
- conversations
- memory
- tools
- repositories
- documents
- archives
- external knowledge structures

Determine whether AI is described as merely storing thought or as actively:

- comparing thoughts
- reconnecting fragments
- returning unfinished questions
- revealing patterns
- restructuring language
- extending the reach of human thinking
- changing what can be remembered or understood

Distinguish between:

```text
external memory
extended cognition
shared workflow
shared identity
relational intelligence
```

Do not assume these are identical.

